{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":2,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1474373611,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE3OlJlbmFtZWRUaXRsZUV2ZW50Nzk1NTQ3NzMw"},"title":"Should save be meta-aware?","was":"Should save be meta-aware?"},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1474829096,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI0OTQzODY4Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/860#issuecomment-249438682"},"message":"This could a can of worms. What is something that is guaranteed to next affect meta data? We might end up aggregating all the time.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1474844313,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI0OTQ1MjExNA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/860#issuecomment-249452114"},"message":"Unless we know which files are related to metadata... And we kinda do, so let's keep it in mind for now at least.\nAnd then it could also generalize to the superdataset meta save since it would know which metadata files to see changed","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1507447604,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzNDk4ODU1Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/860#issuecomment-334988552"},"message":"With #1630 the metadata parser can now be instructed with files to care about, but there is no concept of incremental metadata updates WITHIN a dataset (just across). At the same time the potential runtime delay can only go up with more and more complex parsers. OTOH `save` is called ALL the time. I am 100% confident that nobody wants to pay this price -- in general.\n\nIf desired in some specific scenario though, the `--run-after` config switch could be used to run metadata aggregation after `save()`. `aggregate-metadata` will not alter a dataset unless metadata-relevant pieces have changed. It probably won't work out of the box right now, but in principle this is the way I would achieve this.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1507447604,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTI4MzEwMDY3OQ=="},"status":2},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1507472768,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzNTAxMDE2MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/860#issuecomment-335010160"},"message":"Aggregate-metadata isn't a plugin, but a command ;-) (still not sure what is the fundamental difference besides the visibility etc). I think we will keep running into this until there would be more automagic solution, so I would prefer to keep this one open","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1507472768,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEzOlJlb3BlbmVkRXZlbnQxMjgzMTk5MTcy"},"status":1},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1508071785,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzNjcwOTQ0Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/861#issuecomment-336709447"},"message":"Indeed. This is solved via an option.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1508071785,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTI5MzczMTE2MA=="},"status":2}]}